Perspective, what's the point? (get it...)

So, we've covered angle, tone, and even narrative. We know what we're making, why, and for whom. We have in mind a few ways to spin it and we have even played around with weird ways to deliver the message effectively. What else is there to consider?

Perspective is everything friends. You distill a persona from insights about what someone wants, needs, or struggles with. You've planned the ways they might best receive the great news about your solution. But, don't you think the POV from which the message is delivered has a pretty signficant impact on who watches and why? 

I split perspective out because it can be broken down in so many ways. I'll start listing, and we can go from there. 

1. Brand vs Brand Ambassador
2. Creator vs Influencer
3. Demographics
4. Lifestage
5. Stage in the shopping cycle

Who you choose to represent your brand, and pitch this perfectly crafted story matters. The same story delivered by different people could transform it for better, or for worse. Also, depending on who detailed your persona is, there might be groups of people within it that look pretty different. Don't you think they might respond better to someone who looks and feels like them? Especially when we get into the world of contracting others to film content from your brand, the girls who get it....get it. And the girls who don't will take your money without delivering any real value for how much they cost.

Let's start working through my list, and then I'll dive a bit deeper into the nuances I haven't surfaced yet.
